\begin{question}[ID=\the\value{numA}]\SetQuestionProperties{section-title=\nameref{sec:units}}
%TAG= 201
Sodium ammonium sulfate (\ce{NaNH4SO4}) is a double salt containing ammonium, sodium, and sulfate ions. This salt acts as a water-soluble source of sodium, ammonium, and sulfate ions in specialized chemical synthesis or crystallization experiments. Obtain the net ionic equation for the sodium ammonium sulfate formation:
	\begin{center}\ce{  NaHSO4_{(aq)} + NH3_{(aq)} -> NaNH4SO4_{(aq)}   }  \end{center}	
\end{question}
\begin{solution}
  \ce{   HSO4^-_{(aq)} + NH3_{(aq)}  ->  NH4^+_{(aq)} + SO4^{2-}_{(aq)}    }
   \hspace{0.1cm}\end{solution}\stepcounter{numA}


